{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"How do I troubleshoot issues with the Amazon VPC CNI add-on for Amazon EKS?","context":"### Check the add-on component versions\n\nIt's a best practice to update the core components to the latest version. If the add-on version doesn't match your Kubernetes cluster version, then the add-on can't initialize. Make sure that the [add-on version is compatible with the Kubernetes cluster version](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/managing-vpc-cni.html#vpc-cni-latest-available-version)","url":"https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/eks-troubleshoot-vpc-cni-add-on"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Amazon VPC CNI","context":"### Routinely Upgrade CNI Version\n\nThe VPC CNI is backward compatible. The latest version works with all Amazon EKS supported Kubernetes versions. Additionally, the VPC CNI is offered as an EKS add-on (see \"Deploy VPC CNI Managed Add-On\" above). While EKS add-ons orchestrates upgrades of add-ons, it will not automatically upgrade add-ons like the CNI because they run on the data plane. You are responsible for upgrading the VPC CNI add-on following managed and self-managed worker node upgrades","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/best-practices/vpc-cni.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Assign IPs to Pods with the Amazon VPC CNI","context":"## Amazon VPC CNI versions\n\n| Kubernetes version | Amazon EKS type of VPC CNI version |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1.37 | v1.23.2-eksbuild.12 |\n| 1.36 | v1.23.2-eksbuild.12 |\n| 1.35 | v1.23.2-eksbuild.12 |\n| 1.34 | v1.23.2-eksbuild.12 |\n| 1.33 | v1.23.2-eksbuild.12 |\n| 1.32 | v1.23.2-eksbuild.12 |\n| 1.31 | v1.23.2-eksbuild.12 |\n\nImportant\n\n**Note:**\n\nIf you’re self-managing this add-on, the versions in the table might not be the same as the available self-managed versions. For more information about updating the self-managed type of this add-on, see Update the Amazon VPC CNI (self-managed add-on).\n\nImportant\n\n**Note:**\n\nTo upgrade to VPC CNI v1.12.0 or later, you must upgrade to VPC CNI v1.7.0 first. We recommend that you update one minor version at a time","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/managing-vpc-cni.html"}]}}

